irect"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 against main is open with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Fix:** `src/money.py` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding. I changed `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, so 2.665 now rounds to 2.66 and 2.675 to 2.68, which is what the test expects. The fix is on branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** the request to open the PR timed out, but the PR had actually been created. When I checked the open PRs, it had no reviewers, so I added alex separately.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool says that ID doesn't exist. I went by the test and the docstring, which both specify banker's rounding. The PR hasn't been merged; that needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}